Package: PredSEM
Type: Package
Title: Simple Structural Equation Modeling for Predictive Studies
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person("Jose", "Ventura-Leon", email = "jventuraleon@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2996-4244"))
Description: A small set of functions, one per step of the analysis, for
    predictive or explanatory studies with latent variables. It prepares the
    raw survey data (eligibility criteria, participant flow, reverse items,
    flat responses), describes item responses, fits the measurement model of
    each scale with reliability, describes scores and correlations, estimates
    the structural model with discriminant validity and automatic indirect
    effects, compares rival models, tests measurement invariance and
    multigroup paths, and runs sensitivity analyses. Latent variables are
    defined with short text such as "ASS" or "BERQ1:BERQ4 | BERQ5:BERQ8", and
    hypotheses with formulas such as "SAT ~ ADA + AUT". Every result prints a
    table and a plain-language reading of its key values.
